  "rationale": "The definitive tenor saxophone summit meeting. Two foundational figures of the jazz tradition — Coleman Hawkins, the father of the tenor saxophone, and Ben Webster, the master of the ballad — matched wits with the Oscar Peterson trio at Capitol Studios in October 1957. Consensus across all major canon traditions: Penguin Guide 4★, AllMusic 4★, DownBeat 3.5★, Rolling Stone Jazz Record Guide 4★. A defining statement of the mainstream tradition and a Verve landmark. Fills a major artist gap: neither Hawkins nor Webster has a single album in the current canon.",
