    "notes": "Recorded in one session at Capitol Tower (opened April 1956) — the Capitol Records Studio Melrose Avenue had been superseded by this point. Engineer Val Valentin is inferred from Verve/Capitol engineering credits of the era (Tracking Angle review confirms 'Engineered By: Val Valentin' for Verve reissues from this session). Originally released in November 1959. Also known as 'Blue Saxophones' in the UK. Hawkins recorded 'The Genius of Coleman Hawkins' on the same day with the same rhythm section."
